From 8046808eb9397f88b275bf826d2533bc7f5b6fe1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonn Smith <jonn@broad.mit.edu>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:33:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: don't abort on genotypes with no FORMAT/AD in
 dominant-allele mode

The dominant-allele BCF reader hard-errored (NumericaValueEmptyInt) when
a sample had no AD data, aborting whole-cohort conversions where any
sample lacks coverage at any site. "No AD" is ambiguous (no coverage vs
hom-ref), so:

* AD values entirely absent: consult FORMAT/GT, the honest signal
  (./. -> missing, hom call -> that allele, het/partial -> missing).
* GT absent too: new --absent-ad-as {missing|ref} flag decides, default
  missing. "ref" fabricates calls and is only for callsets whose
  convention is "no AD means reference" (not GATK joint callsets, where
  covered hom-refs carry real AD). Also settable as absent_ad_as in the
  --bcf-filter-config toml (serde default: missing), so the in-tree
  bcf2hmmibd converter gains it without driver changes.
* AD present but all zero (e.g. 0,0): missing, as before (previously
  fell out of the NaN ratio compare), GT not consulted since AD
  explicitly says zero reads.
* Guard the latent indv_ad[0]/[1] panics and the 0/0 NaN ratio.

A missing value inside an otherwise present AD vector counts as 0 reads.
GT-resolved calls count toward min_site_nonmissing like AD-based calls.

Note: --bcf-to-bin-file output is not byte-compatible across this change
(BcfFilterArgs gained a field); regenerate bin files rather than mixing
versions. On AD-complete data output is unchanged: full-run hmm.txt and
hmm_fract.txt on testdata/pf7_data are identical to v0.1.7's.

Fixture testdata/absent_ad/absent_ad.bcf (generator script alongside)
covers all branches; old binary reproduces the abort on it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
